window.US_GAME_PREVIEWS={"asOf":"2026-10-16","method":"Based on official results, available player box scores and credited school reporting. Team averages are not adjusted for strength of schedule.","games":[{"id":"2026-10-16-calgary-ubc","away":"calgary","home":"ubc","date":"2026-10-16","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"UBC gets another shot at Calgary after opening loss","paragraphs":["UBC has won three games since Calgary held it to seven points in the season opener. None of those wins will help much Friday if the Thunderbirds let the Dinos do it again.","“We have secured nothing,” head coach Blake Nill told UBC Athletics this week. At 3–2, the Thunderbirds are ahead of Calgary in wins, but a second loss to the Dinos would erase that advantage.","The offence looks better equipped for the rematch than it did in the 23–7 opener. Marvyn Larozar ran for 137 yards and a touchdown against Saskatchewan, and Drew Viotto added two touchdown passes. The trouble was that UBC still lost 34–24, with two Viotto interceptions contributing to another afternoon that slipped away.","Calgary's last game showed the value of avoiding those mistakes. David Jordan wasn't intercepted in a 14–13 win over Regina, giving the Dinos a result after consecutive losses in which they had scored 36 and 35 points.","That leaves UBC facing an opponent it cannot measure solely by scoring averages. Calgary has already beaten the Thunderbirds with defence and just won another close game the same way. Larozar's running gives UBC a way to make the return meeting different, provided the rest of the offence doesn't give those gains back."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-16","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_bx7n.xml","label":"September 4 · UBC at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_96n6.xml","label":"September 19 · Calgary at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260925_jbqx.xml","label":"September 25 · Alberta at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_y81r.xml","label":"September 18 · Regina at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_8tvd.xml","label":"October 3 · UBC at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-british-columbia/boxscore/8947","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/9303","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/6999","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://www.reginacougars.com/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc/boxscore/11425","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gothunderbirds.ca/news/2026/10/14/football-navacord-bc-insurance-preview-t-birds-host-dinos-for-key-shot-at-redemption.aspx","label":"UBC Thunderbirds · pregame reporting"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/regina/boxscore/15530","label":"2026-10-03 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-16-manitoba-saskatchewan","away":"manitoba","home":"saskatchewan","date":"2026-10-16","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Huskies seek payback against Bisons in Saskatoon","paragraphs":["When Manitoba beat Saskatchewan to open the season, the Huskies left Winnipeg with a 40–22 loss and plenty to repair. Four straight wins later, they can secure a playoff berth by beating the same team Friday in Saskatoon.","That would give the rematch a fitting ending for Saskatchewan, which has scored 65, 38 and 34 points in its last three games. Against UBC, Anton Amundrud threw for 295 yards while Aulain Penner ran for two touchdowns, helping the Huskies find enough offence for a 34–24 win.","Manitoba has already shown it can keep Saskatchewan from getting the result it wants, but the Bisons haven't been as steady since the opener. A 31–6 loss to UBC was followed by an 18–3 win over Alberta, leaving them 3–2 as both teams return from the conference bye.","The Alberta game offers Manitoba a more useful approach to the rematch. Ishe Matanga rushed for 122 yards, allowing the Bisons to win without needing a big passing total from Cole Anseeuw.","If Manitoba can keep possessions moving that way, Amundrud and the Huskies will have fewer chances to continue their scoring run. If it cannot, Saskatchewan's offence has spent four games showing why the opener may no longer be the best guide to this matchup."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-16","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_gdvt.xml","label":"September 5 · Saskatchewan at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_hvcf.xml","label":"September 11 · Manitoba at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_96n6.xml","label":"September 19 · Calgary at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_mge2.xml","label":"September 18 · Saskatchewan at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_8tvd.xml","label":"October 3 · UBC at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-saskatchewan/boxscore/8948","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan-huskies/boxscore/9300","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan/boxscore/15527","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/regina-rams/boxscore/6998","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/6999","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/news/2026/10/15/football-no-3-huskies-eye-postseason-clinch-in-rematch-with-manitoba.aspx","label":"Saskatchewan Huskies · pregame reporting"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-manitoba/boxscore/8950","label":"2026-10-02 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-bishops-sherbrooke","away":"bishops","home":"sherbrooke","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gaiters, Vert & Or look for a much-needed win","paragraphs":["Sherbrooke finally made one of the RSEQ's stronger teams work for a win. Now the Vert & Or have to carry that performance into a game they have a better chance of winning themselves.","Their 23–17 loss to Montréal followed defeats of 55–24 against Laval and 34–1 against McGill. It wasn't enough to get Sherbrooke out of the win column's zero, but Jeremy Fyfe's 310 passing yards gave the offence something more substantial to show for the afternoon.","Saturday's opponent, Bishop's, arrives with a similar problem: an improved passing performance that did not produce an improved result. Mathieu Bellavance threw two touchdown passes without an interception against McGill, only for the Gaiters to lose 47–27.","That leaves Bishop's at 1–4 and Sherbrooke at 0–5, with both offences trying to turn a better outing into something that lasts. The Gaiters had scored just 14 points in their previous two games before reaching 27 against McGill.","Sherbrooke's defence kept Montréal within reach; Bishop's offence gave its team more points to work with. Neither improvement has yet delivered a win. Their meeting offers a chance to put the two halves of a performance together."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Sherbrooke at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_shbp.xml","label":"September 26 · Concordia at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_8v74.xml","label":"September 26 · McGill at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12462","label":"2026-10-04 · Official player box score"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_zz6y.xml","label":"2026-10-03 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-carleton-laurier","away":"carleton","home":"laurier","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Ravens chase first win on road at Laurier","paragraphs":["Laurier got three touchdown passes and no interceptions from Will Russell against Waterloo. That should have made for a good afternoon. Instead, the Golden Hawks gave up 39 points and came away with another loss.","Saturday's visit from Carleton is a chance to make better use of an offence that has been doing enough to keep Laurier competitive. Russell passed for 296 yards in the Waterloo game, with Ryan Hughes catching two touchdowns, but the 39–31 defeat left the Hawks 2–4.","Carleton knows the feeling of scoring enough to stay close without collecting the win. The Ravens lost 35–32 to Ottawa before Western beat them 49–7, leaving them winless through six games.","The Ottawa result is the one Laurier will want to keep in mind. Carleton has averaged 21.8 points despite its record, and a Golden Hawks defence allowing 27.7 cannot assume the Ravens will be as quiet as they were against Western.","Russell and Hughes have already shown they can supply points. Whether Laurier turns those points into a win will depend on keeping Carleton from finding the kind of offensive afternoon that nearly carried it past the Gee-Gees."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_y7d5.xml","label":"August 29 · Carleton at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_o8yt.xml","label":"September 6 · Waterloo at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_jbsa.xml","label":"September 12 · Carleton at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_o7bu.xml","label":"September 19 · Queen's at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_yqpv.xml","label":"October 4 · Carleton at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_e02s.xml","label":"October 10 · Western at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_zyoz.xml","label":"August 29 · Guelph at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_tqi8.xml","label":"September 6 · Laurier at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Ottawa at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_r1pc.xml","label":"September 19 · Laurier at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_onmm.xml","label":"September 26 · York at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_3xzq.xml","label":"October 3 · Laurier at Waterloo"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-guelph-queens","away":"guelph","home":"queens","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gaels look to rebound as Gryphons visit Kingston","paragraphs":["Queen's went into last weekend trying to protect an unbeaten record. It goes into this one trying to keep its first loss from becoming the start of something more troubling.","Guelph visits Kingston on Saturday with three straight wins and an offence that has scored 124 points during that run. That is an awkward opponent for a Gaels team coming off a 25–22 loss to Windsor.","The Gaels were without Hec Crighton Watch quarterback Alex Vreeken against Windsor, as reported by 3DownNation. Ashton St. Germain handled all 26 pass attempts in his place, finishing with 280 yards, a touchdown and three interceptions. Getting Vreeken back would give Queen's a different starting point for its response, though the report did not give a return date.","The Gryphons have been getting a much happier return from their passing game. Tristan Aboud threw four touchdown passes in a 46–0 win over Toronto, twice finding Willem Arseneau for scores. That production has put Aboud on CanUFootball's Hec Crighton Watch and helped turn a 1–2 start into a 4–2 record.","Toronto offered less resistance than Queen's is likely to provide. But Guelph had already won a close game against Ottawa and scored 47 against Waterloo before the shutout, giving the winning streak more substance than one big afternoon.","For the 5–1 Gaels, that is what makes Saturday consequential. Windsor ended their perfect start. A Guelph win would bring the Gryphons level with them in victories and turn last week's setback into a much tighter OUA race."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_zyoz.xml","label":"August 29 · Guelph at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_zejw.xml","label":"September 6 · McMaster at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_jbsa.xml","label":"September 12 · Carleton at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hkpj.xml","label":"September 19 · Guelph at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_pvm1.xml","label":"September 26 · Waterloo at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_07bf.xml","label":"October 3 · Guelph at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260830_q4gr.xml","label":"August 30 · Queen's at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_pii8.xml","label":"September 12 · Waterloo at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_o7bu.xml","label":"September 19 · Queen's at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_2hsv.xml","label":"September 26 · Ottawa at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_7san.xml","label":"October 3 · Queen's at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_11lr.xml","label":"October 10 · Windsor at Queen's"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/carleton-ravens/boxscore/13808","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/ottawa-gee-gees/boxscore/13809","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/toronto-varsity-blues/boxscore/13806","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/waterloo-warriors/boxscore/13807","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/western-mustangs/boxscore/13810","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/carleton-ravens/boxscore/9559","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laurier-golden-hawks/boxscore/9557","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/mcmaster-marauders/boxscore/9558","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ottawa-gee-gees/boxscore/9560","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/toronto-varsity-blues/boxscore/9562","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/news/2026/10/10/queens-football-drop-tight-contest-to-windsor.aspx","label":"Queen’s Athletics · October 10 game report"},{"url":"https://3downnation.com/2026/10/10/around-u-sports-windsor-lancers-hand-queens-gaels-first-loss/","label":"3DownNation · Vreeken absent against Windsor"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-mcmaster-waterloo","away":"mcmaster","home":"waterloo","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Marauders take stingy defence into Waterloo","paragraphs":["Nathan Denkers had a 102-yard receiving day in McMaster's last win, but his thoughts afterward were on the points the Marauders had left behind.","“Finishing the drives is a huge point of emphasis for us,” he told McMaster Athletics after a 26–6 win over Toronto. It was an understandable concern on an afternoon when Lucas Barresi threw two touchdown passes but was also intercepted four times.","McMaster's defence made sure those mistakes did not cost the game. The Marauders have allowed just 15.7 points a game on their way to a 5–1 record, repeatedly giving the offence another chance when a possession ends badly.","Waterloo has had to live much closer to the opposite extreme. The Warriors allowed 44 points to Windsor and 47 to Guelph before beating Laurier 39–31, a result that took a productive day from Brandon Riggan on the ground and Tyler Tierney through the air to reach 2–4.","That makes Saturday a chance for McMaster to address exactly what Denkers identified. Waterloo has been giving opponents scoring opportunities. The Marauders' defence has kept them from needing to finish all of theirs, but they would prefer not to keep testing how far that protection can carry them."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_uxji.xml","label":"August 29 · Windsor at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_zejw.xml","label":"September 6 · McMaster at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_y44l.xml","label":"September 12 · McMaster at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_r1pc.xml","label":"September 19 · Laurier at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_xfxk.xml","label":"September 26 · McMaster at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261009_44ma.xml","label":"October 9 · Toronto at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_rmtf.xml","label":"August 29 · Ottawa at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_o8yt.xml","label":"September 6 · Waterloo at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_pii8.xml","label":"September 12 · Waterloo at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_ed0b.xml","label":"September 19 · Windsor at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_pvm1.xml","label":"September 26 · Waterloo at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_3xzq.xml","label":"October 3 · Laurier at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://marauders.ca/news/2026/10/9/football-marauders-claim-inaugural-battle-of-lake-ontario-with-26-6-win-over-toronto.aspx","label":"McMaster Athletics · October 9 game report"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-saint-marys-acadia","away":"saint-marys","home":"acadia","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Unbeaten Huskies visit Axemen in AUS rematch","paragraphs":["Acadia threw for 247 yards without an interception the last time it faced Saint Mary's. It still scored only seven points. That is the problem the Axemen have to solve when the unbeaten Huskies visit Saturday.","Mason Jude found Jase LeBlanc for 104 receiving yards and a touchdown in the October 2 meeting, but Saint Mary's won 24–7. The passing yards gave Acadia movement without giving it enough points to put the Huskies under pressure.","That left Saint Mary's free to lean on Malcolm Bussey, who rushed for 124 yards and a touchdown. His production helped the Huskies win their second meeting of the season after a 29–16 result in September.","Acadia has now lost three straight, with a 38–12 defeat against StFX between those Saint Mary's games. At 1–4, the Axemen have found the AUS's stronger defences difficult to turn over for touchdowns even when the offence manages some useful gains.","The Huskies are 5–0 and allowing just 12.2 points a game. Acadia already knows it can complete passes against them. Saturday's challenge is making those completions change the score before Bussey and the Saint Mary's offence put the game beyond reach again."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_olce.xml","label":"September 5 · Saint Mary's at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_aecb.xml","label":"September 11 · Mount Allison at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_vzdr.xml","label":"September 19 · Saint Mary's at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_e8ye.xml","label":"September 26 · Saint Mary's at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_b8gs.xml","label":"October 2 · Acadia at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_m54m.xml","label":"September 4 · Acadia at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_s8sj.xml","label":"September 12 · Acadia at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_6175.xml","label":"September 26 · StFX at Acadia"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-stfx-mount-allison","away":"stfx","home":"mount-allison","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Mounties look for answers against surging X-Men","paragraphs":["Mount Allison has seen enough of StFX's offence lately to know the names. Stopping them has been another matter.","The X-Men have beaten the Mounties 42–6 and 44–14 in their last three outings, with a win over Acadia between the two. That run has taken StFX to 3–2 and put 124 points on the board.","The most recent meeting showed why the Mounties have struggled to slow it down. Deion Blackwood threw for 275 yards and two touchdowns, Aiden Rossong ran for two more scores, and Ayres Perry finished with 111 receiving yards. Taking away one part of that attack would still have left Mount Allison with plenty to defend.","Spencer Joudry gave the Mounties a touchdown pass without an interception, but it made little difference in a game that demanded far more offence. Mount Allison did stay much closer to Saint Mary's in a 24–17 loss between the StFX meetings.","That is the sort of game the 1–4 Mounties need to create Saturday. The trouble is that StFX has scored 86 points in their two meetings, more than Mount Allison has scored all season through five games. The X-Men have given them very little time to settle into a closer contest."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_olce.xml","label":"September 5 · Saint Mary's at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_s8sj.xml","label":"September 12 · Acadia at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_2r1j.xml","label":"September 19 · StFX at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_6175.xml","label":"September 26 · StFX at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_n4x7.xml","label":"October 3 · Mount Allison at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_m54m.xml","label":"September 4 · Acadia at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_aecb.xml","label":"September 11 · Mount Allison at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_e8ye.xml","label":"September 26 · Saint Mary's at Mount Allison"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-western-ottawa","away":"western","home":"ottawa","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gee-Gees face Western after setback against York","paragraphs":["Ottawa's offence moved the ball against York last week. What it could not do was turn enough of that movement into points, an expensive habit to carry into a game against Western.","Josh Janssen passed for 262 yards in the Gee-Gees' 19–12 loss, leaving Ottawa 4–3. Saturday's visitors have been averaging 49 points a game, so another afternoon stuck at 12 would leave the Gee-Gees asking their defence for an enormous rescue.","Western made that danger clear against Carleton. Ethan Dolby rushed for 140 yards, while Ben Casselman threw three touchdown passes in a 49–7 win. The Mustangs did not need to choose between running through the Ravens and throwing past them.","That win also gave Western an immediate answer to its 41–30 loss to Queen's. Even in defeat, the Mustangs had reached 30 points; they are 5–1 because most opponents have not been able to ask for much more than that.","Ottawa's recent win over Carleton came by only three points. The Gee-Gees can score enough to make a game close, but York showed what happens when their drives produce too little. Western is unlikely to leave them as much room to recover."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_bmmb.xml","label":"September 6 · York at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_nlwf.xml","label":"September 12 · Western at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_qrnw.xml","label":"September 19 · Western at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_xfxk.xml","label":"September 26 · McMaster at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_7san.xml","label":"October 3 · Queen's at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_e02s.xml","label":"October 10 · Western at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_rmtf.xml","label":"August 29 · Ottawa at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_kxlu.xml","label":"September 5 · Toronto at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Ottawa at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hkpj.xml","label":"September 19 · Guelph at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_2hsv.xml","label":"September 26 · Ottawa at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_yqpv.xml","label":"October 4 · Carleton at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-10","label":"October 10 · Ottawa at York"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/western-mustangs/boxscore/13810","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-mustangs/boxscore/6119","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://marauders.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-university/boxscore/14057","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://varsityblues.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-university/boxscore/12855","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://westernmustangs.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/york-lions/boxscore/17092","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_kodd.xml","label":"2026-10-10 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-york-toronto","away":"york","home":"toronto","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Lions seek another win as Blues look for breakthrough","paragraphs":["York did not suddenly become a polished offensive team when it beat Ottawa. Maurice Sodja threw two interceptions, and the Lions still needed his work on the ground to get enough points. What changed was that their defence finally made those points enough.","The 19–12 win took York to 2–4 after consecutive defeats against Laurier and Windsor. Sodja rushed for 51 yards and a touchdown, giving the Lions a way to survive an uneven passing day.","Saturday's opponent, Toronto, has been waiting for a similar change in fortune. The Varsity Blues have scored six points in their last three games, leaving them 0–6 and their defence with little margin to work with.","Omarion Martin rushed for 69 yards against McMaster, but Toronto lost 26–6. That came after shutouts against Windsor and Guelph, a sequence that has made every promising drive feel more important than the last.","York has not scored freely either, averaging 13.2 points. The difference is that the Lions now have a recent example of winning without doing so. Toronto is still looking for the afternoon when a few scoring drives and enough stops finally arrive together."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_y7d5.xml","label":"August 29 · Carleton at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_bmmb.xml","label":"September 6 · York at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_y44l.xml","label":"September 12 · McMaster at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_onmm.xml","label":"September 26 · York at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_dr1h.xml","label":"October 3 · York at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-10","label":"October 10 · Ottawa at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260830_q4gr.xml","label":"August 30 · Queen's at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_kxlu.xml","label":"September 5 · Toronto at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_qrnw.xml","label":"September 19 · Western at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_1coy.xml","label":"September 26 · Toronto at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_07bf.xml","label":"October 3 · Guelph at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261009_44ma.xml","label":"October 9 · Toronto at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_kodd.xml","label":"2026-10-10 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-18-mcgill-laval","away":"mcgill","home":"laval","date":"2026-10-18","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"McGill takes winning run into showdown with Laval","paragraphs":["McGill's three-game winning streak has brought it within one win of Laval. Keeping that streak alive Sunday would do something even more useful: put the first loss on the Rouge et Or's record.","The difficulty is that Laval has been getting better at scoring as the schedule has gone on. Its last three games have produced 145 points, most recently a 48–15 win over Concordia in which Olivier Cool caught three touchdown passes from Victor Charland.","McGill has scored 110 over its own three-game run, so this is not a visitor arriving without an offence. Elliott Drapeau accounted for three touchdowns against Bishop's, two passing and one rushing, while the Redbirds have also had the season-long running threat of Jerry Momo.","That gives McGill ways to keep possessions going. It may need them against a Laval attack that has averaged 39 points, because handing the ball back quickly would give Charland and Cool more chances to repeat what they did to Concordia.","The defensive averages offer McGill some encouragement: it has allowed 17 points a game to Laval's 17.2. The Redbirds have earned a 4–1 record partly by making opponents work for their scoring. At 5–0, Laval brings the clearest test yet of how far that defence can carry the winning streak."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-18","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_60uu.xml","label":"September 11 · Laval at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_8v74.xml","label":"September 26 · McGill at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_3enl.xml","label":"September 26 · Montréal at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12458","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12462","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/concordia-shaughnessy-cup-/boxscore/12460","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laval-tva-/boxscore/12459","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/sherbrooke/boxscore/12461","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-23-alberta-saskatchewan","away":"alberta","home":"saskatchewan","date":"2026-10-23","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Golden Bears face return trip to Saskatchewan","paragraphs":["Alberta's first meeting with Saskatchewan became the kind of game a team would rather leave behind. The Huskies scored 65 points, and the Golden Bears spent the afternoon trying to find a response that never came.","The 65–12 defeat matters to the return trip because Saskatchewan has kept scoring since then. Wins over Regina and UBC followed, with Anton Amundrud throwing for 295 yards and Aulain Penner rushing for two touchdowns against the Thunderbirds.","Alberta has produced one encouraging answer of its own, a 42–35 win over Calgary. But the next game brought only three points against Manitoba, making it difficult to know how much of that scoring the Bears can bring into another demanding assignment.","Eli Hetlinger was intercepted twice in the Manitoba loss. Against a Saskatchewan offence averaging 40.6 points through five games, those lost possessions would be particularly difficult to absorb. Alberta does not need the rematch to resemble its win over Calgary in every respect. It does need to avoid giving the Huskies another game in which almost all of the scoring belongs to them."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-23","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_pg8n.xml","label":"September 4 · Regina at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_mge2.xml","label":"September 18 · Saskatchewan at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260925_jbqx.xml","label":"September 25 · Alberta at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_gdvt.xml","label":"September 5 · Saskatchewan at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_8tvd.xml","label":"October 3 · UBC at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-saskatchewan/boxscore/8948","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan-huskies/boxscore/9300","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan/boxscore/15527","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/regina-rams/boxscore/6998","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/6999","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-manitoba/boxscore/8950","label":"2026-10-02 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-23-mount-allison-saint-marys","away":"mount-allison","home":"saint-marys","date":"2026-10-23","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Mounties take another run at Huskies","paragraphs":["Mount Allison came closer to beating Saint Mary's than its other recent results would suggest. Between two heavy losses to StFX, the Mounties kept the Huskies within a touchdown in a 24–17 game.","That gives the return meeting a more useful starting point than Mount Allison's 1–4 record alone. The Mounties did not need to match Saint Mary's with a string of big offensive plays to stay involved; they needed to keep the score low enough that their own drives still mattered.","It is a difficult balance against a team with Malcolm Bussey carrying the ball. He rushed for 124 yards and a touchdown in Saint Mary's latest win over Acadia, helping the Huskies control a game in which their defence allowed only seven points.","The Mounties have been able to find receiving yards through Quinten George, who had 96 against StFX, but that game showed the limits of chasing a large deficit. Their closer meeting with Saint Mary's offers a different route. Keeping Bussey from letting the Huskies settle into control would make George's catches worth more than a contribution to the yardage total."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-23","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_m54m.xml","label":"September 4 · Acadia at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_aecb.xml","label":"September 11 · Mount Allison at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_2r1j.xml","label":"September 19 · StFX at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_e8ye.xml","label":"September 26 · Saint Mary's at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_n4x7.xml","label":"October 3 · Mount Allison at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_olce.xml","label":"September 5 · Saint Mary's at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_vzdr.xml","label":"September 19 · Saint Mary's at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_b8gs.xml","label":"October 2 · Acadia at Saint Mary's"}]},{"id":"2026-10-23-ubc-regina","away":"ubc","home":"regina","date":"2026-10-23","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Thunderbirds, Rams meet again after close finish","paragraphs":["Regina's first meeting with UBC ended with the Rams five points short. The frustration since then is that they have kept getting close without changing the result.","A 38–31 loss to Saskatchewan and a 14–13 loss to Calgary followed the 25–20 defeat against the Thunderbirds. The Rams' defence has allowed only 18.6 points a game, enough to keep them involved without delivering the wins their 2–3 record needs.","Against Calgary, Carter Ashman ran for 110 yards, but Owen Sieben was intercepted three times. That is the sort of offensive day Regina cannot afford to repeat against UBC, where Marvyn Larozar gives the Thunderbirds a way to keep the ball and make empty opposing possessions costly.","Larozar ran for 137 yards in UBC's loss to Saskatchewan, so the Thunderbirds know that a productive ground game alone does not settle anything either. Both teams have recently watched good rushing performances disappear into defeats. Their return meeting is a chance to put that work together with the cleaner passing and timely stops that were missing."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-23","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_bx7n.xml","label":"September 4 · UBC at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_y81r.xml","label":"September 18 · Regina at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_8tvd.xml","label":"October 3 · UBC at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_pg8n.xml","label":"September 4 · Regina at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_hvcf.xml","label":"September 11 · Manitoba at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-british-columbia/boxscore/8947","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/9303","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/6999","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://www.reginacougars.com/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc/boxscore/11425","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/regina/boxscore/15530","label":"2026-10-03 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-acadia-stfx","away":"acadia","home":"stfx","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Axemen seek better result against X-Men","paragraphs":["Acadia has been able to complete passes against the AUS's stronger teams. Turning them into enough points has been another matter, and its return meeting with StFX puts that problem back in view.","The X-Men won the first game 38–12. Acadia then got 247 passing yards from Mason Jude against Saint Mary's but scored only seven, leaving the Axemen with another afternoon in which useful gains did not make the opponent uncomfortable.","StFX has been making much more of its possessions. Against Mount Allison, Deion Blackwood threw two touchdown passes and Aiden Rossong rushed for two more, giving the X-Men production through both parts of the offence.","That helps explain why Acadia needs more than a respectable passing total in the rematch. StFX has scored 124 points during a three-game winning streak. If Jude's completions keep ending without touchdowns, Blackwood and Rossong will get the chance to pull away before the Axemen's yardage can mean very much."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_m54m.xml","label":"September 4 · Acadia at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_s8sj.xml","label":"September 12 · Acadia at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_vzdr.xml","label":"September 19 · Saint Mary's at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_6175.xml","label":"September 26 · StFX at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_b8gs.xml","label":"October 2 · Acadia at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_olce.xml","label":"September 5 · Saint Mary's at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_2r1j.xml","label":"September 19 · StFX at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_n4x7.xml","label":"October 3 · Mount Allison at StFX"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-concordia-sherbrooke","away":"concordia","home":"sherbrooke","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Stingers, Vert & Or meet with offence under scrutiny","paragraphs":["Concordia and Sherbrooke have both had recent games in which the passing numbers looked more encouraging than the scoreboard. Their meeting gives each a chance to turn that small improvement into something more useful.","For the Stingers, it was Ely Rivest's 117 receiving yards against Laval. He added a touchdown, but Concordia lost 48–15, leaving an offence averaging 11 points a game with another individual performance instead of a competitive result.","Sherbrooke got closer. Jeremy Fyfe passed for 310 yards in a 23–17 loss to Montréal, giving the Vert & Or enough offence to stay involved after much heavier defeats against Laval and McGill.","That makes Sherbrooke's most recent game the more encouraging model for this matchup. Neither side has been scoring freely enough to count on winning a race. If Fyfe can keep the Vert & Or moving, Concordia will need Rivest's catches to produce more than another good line in a losing box score. The Stingers' only win so far came with ten points; they would prefer not to depend on that being enough again."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_ppda.xml","label":"September 12 · Montréal at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_shbp.xml","label":"September 26 · Concordia at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Sherbrooke at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_8v74.xml","label":"September 26 · McGill at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_zz6y.xml","label":"2026-10-03 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-laurier-western","away":"laurier","home":"western","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Golden Hawks face high-scoring Mustangs","paragraphs":["Laurier's loss to Waterloo showed how little an efficient passing day can mean without enough stops. Will Russell threw three touchdowns without an interception, and the Golden Hawks still lost 39–31.","That is a worrying result to carry toward a meeting with Western. The Mustangs have averaged 49 points through six games and have been able to generate them without depending on one part of the offence.","Against Carleton, Ben Casselman threw three touchdown passes while Ethan Dolby rushed for 140 yards. The 49–7 win gave Western an immediate response to its loss to Queen's and left the Ravens unable to make either the run or the pass manageable.","Laurier will want to give Russell a much less demanding job. His 296 passing yards and Ryan Hughes' two touchdown catches against Waterloo were enough to keep the Hawks involved, but not enough to overcome the defensive total. If Western is allowed its usual scoring pace, another clean afternoon from Russell could again end with too little reward."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_zyoz.xml","label":"August 29 · Guelph at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_tqi8.xml","label":"September 6 · Laurier at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Ottawa at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_r1pc.xml","label":"September 19 · Laurier at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_onmm.xml","label":"September 26 · York at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_3xzq.xml","label":"October 3 · Laurier at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_bmmb.xml","label":"September 6 · York at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_nlwf.xml","label":"September 12 · Western at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_qrnw.xml","label":"September 19 · Western at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_xfxk.xml","label":"September 26 · McMaster at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_7san.xml","label":"October 3 · Queen's at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_e02s.xml","label":"October 10 · Western at Carleton"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/western-mustangs/boxscore/13810","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-mustangs/boxscore/6119","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://marauders.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-university/boxscore/14057","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://varsityblues.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-university/boxscore/12855","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://westernmustangs.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/york-lions/boxscore/17092","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-laval-bishops","away":"laval","home":"bishops","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gaiters prepare for another test against Laval","paragraphs":["Bishop's found more passing offence against McGill and still lost by 20. A meeting with Laval offers little comfort if the Gaiters cannot keep that improvement from being swallowed by another large defensive total.","Mathieu Bellavance threw two touchdown passes without an interception in the 47–27 loss. That was progress after Bishop's had managed only nine points against Montréal and five against Concordia, but it did not make the game close enough at the finish.","Laval has been asking even more of opposing offences. The Rouge et Or have scored 145 points in their last three games, including a 48–15 win over Concordia in which Olivier Cool caught three touchdowns from Victor Charland.","Cool's afternoon makes the problem concrete for the Gaiters. Bellavance can avoid interceptions and still watch the score move away if Laval keeps finishing its own drives. Bishop's passing improvement gives it something to build on; against Charland and Cool, the defence has to give that work a chance to count."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_60uu.xml","label":"September 11 · Laval at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_3enl.xml","label":"September 26 · Montréal at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Sherbrooke at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_shbp.xml","label":"September 26 · Concordia at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laval-tva-/boxscore/12459","label":"Victor Charland · player statistics"},{"url":"https://rougeetor.ulaval.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/boxscore-20260905-concordia-laval.pdf","label":"Victor Charland · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12462","label":"2026-10-04 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-manitoba-calgary","away":"manitoba","home":"calgary","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Dinos, Bisons set for rematch after two-point game","paragraphs":["Calgary scored 36 points against Manitoba and still lost. The return meeting gives the Dinos a chance to improve on the part of that game their offence could not solve.","The Bisons won 38–36 in September, leaving very little between the teams apart from one more successful scoring possession. Both have since shown they can play a different kind of game: Calgary beat Regina 14–13, while Manitoba held Alberta to three points in an 18–3 win.","The Bisons' ground game helped make that lower-scoring win possible. Ishe Matanga rushed for 122 yards, allowing Cole Anseeuw to get through the afternoon with 142 passing yards, a touchdown and no interceptions.","Calgary got a similarly clean passing day from David Jordan against Regina, with 215 yards and no interceptions. That is useful preparation for a rematch that need not become another exchange of touchdowns. The Dinos already know they can score against Manitoba. Another controlled offensive day, paired with one more stop than they found in September, would make those points go further."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_gdvt.xml","label":"September 5 · Saskatchewan at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_hvcf.xml","label":"September 11 · Manitoba at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_96n6.xml","label":"September 19 · Calgary at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_bx7n.xml","label":"September 4 · UBC at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260925_jbqx.xml","label":"September 25 · Alberta at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-manitoba/boxscore/8950","label":"2026-10-02 · Official player box score"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/regina/boxscore/15530","label":"2026-10-03 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-montreal-mcgill","away":"montreal","home":"mcgill","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Carabins, Redbirds bring contrasting strengths to rematch","paragraphs":["McGill's running game gives it more than a way to gain yards against Montréal. It offers a way to keep the Carabins' higher-scoring offence waiting on the sideline.","Jerry Momo has rushed for 733 yards in the five games included in CanUFootball's player totals, earning a place on the Hec Crighton Watch. Against Bishop's, quarterback Elliott Drapeau supplied another threat on the ground, rushing for 80 yards and a touchdown to go with two passing scores.","That variety has helped the Redbirds score 110 points during a three-game winning streak. It also gives Montréal more to account for than simply stopping one runner before getting the ball back.","The Carabins know the value of that kind of afternoon. Merton Theagene rushed for 116 yards in their 23–17 win over Sherbrooke, carrying much of the offensive work in a closer game than Montréal's 38.8-point average would suggest.","Both teams are 4–1 through five games. McGill has allowed fewer points, but Montréal has scored more. The running attacks could do more than decide which offence has the better day; they could help decide how many chances the other one gets."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_ppda.xml","label":"September 12 · Montréal at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_3enl.xml","label":"September 26 · Montréal at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_60uu.xml","label":"September 11 · Laval at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_8v74.xml","label":"September 26 · McGill at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12458","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12462","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/concordia-shaughnessy-cup-/boxscore/12460","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laval-tva-/boxscore/12459","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/sherbrooke/boxscore/12461","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_zz6y.xml","label":"2026-10-03 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-queens-mcmaster","away":"queens","home":"mcmaster","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gaels offence meets Marauders defence","paragraphs":["Queen's and McMaster both watched their quarterbacks throw several interceptions in their last games. Only McMaster came away with a win, but the comparison comes with an important detail: the Gaels were missing Hec Crighton Watch quarterback Alex Vreeken, according to 3DownNation.","Ashton St. Germain handled all 26 Queen's pass attempts against Windsor, throwing for 280 yards with three interceptions in the 25–22 loss. The report did not give a return date for Vreeken. McMaster, meanwhile, survived four Lucas Barresi interceptions against Toronto and still won 26–6.","The difference was the protection McMaster got from its defence. The Marauders have allowed 15.7 points a game, giving an offence averaging 24.2 room to survive an untidy possession or two.","Queen's has more scoring power, averaging 39.3, but Windsor showed that the Gaels cannot assume it will erase every mistake. Their previous two games had both produced 41 points; the Lancers kept that attack to 22 and made the close finish count.","At 5–1 each, the teams have found different routes to the same record. Their meeting asks whether Queen's can get its scoring moving again against a defence that has made a habit of giving McMaster another chance."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260830_q4gr.xml","label":"August 30 · Queen's at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_pii8.xml","label":"September 12 · Waterloo at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_o7bu.xml","label":"September 19 · Queen's at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_2hsv.xml","label":"September 26 · Ottawa at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_7san.xml","label":"October 3 · Queen's at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_11lr.xml","label":"October 10 · Windsor at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_uxji.xml","label":"August 29 · Windsor at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_zejw.xml","label":"September 6 · McMaster at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_y44l.xml","label":"September 12 · McMaster at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_r1pc.xml","label":"September 19 · Laurier at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_xfxk.xml","label":"September 26 · McMaster at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261009_44ma.xml","label":"October 9 · Toronto at McMaster"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/carleton-ravens/boxscore/13808","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/ottawa-gee-gees/boxscore/13809","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/toronto-varsity-blues/boxscore/13806","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/waterloo-warriors/boxscore/13807","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/western-mustangs/boxscore/13810","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/news/2026/10/10/queens-football-drop-tight-contest-to-windsor.aspx","label":"Queen’s Athletics · October 10 game report"},{"url":"https://3downnation.com/2026/10/10/around-u-sports-windsor-lancers-hand-queens-gaels-first-loss/","label":"3DownNation · Vreeken absent against Windsor"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-toronto-carleton","away":"toronto","home":"carleton","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Blues, Ravens search for better finish to OUA season","paragraphs":["Carleton has scored enough to come close to a win. Toronto has spent much of the season trying to score enough to make a game close at all.","That difference matters when two teams winless through six games meet. The Ravens took Ottawa to a 35–32 finish, while the Blues have scored only six points in their last three outings.","Toronto got 69 rushing yards from Omarion Martin against McMaster, but lost 26–6. After shutouts against Windsor and Guelph, that was another game in which a useful contribution on the ground did not give the offence enough to work with on the scoreboard.","Carleton's bigger problem has been preserving its own scoring chances with stops. The Ravens have allowed 44.2 points a game, leaving Elijah Barnes and the offence little room for a quiet stretch. Barnes threw for 200 yards against Western but was intercepted twice in a 49–7 loss.","Toronto will try to find points against a defence that has been giving them up. Carleton will try to turn its greater offensive production into the result that nearly arrived against Ottawa. For both, this is a chance to make one of the season's persistent problems less decisive."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260830_q4gr.xml","label":"August 30 · Queen's at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_kxlu.xml","label":"September 5 · Toronto at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_qrnw.xml","label":"September 19 · Western at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_1coy.xml","label":"September 26 · Toronto at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_07bf.xml","label":"October 3 · Guelph at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261009_44ma.xml","label":"October 9 · Toronto at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_y7d5.xml","label":"August 29 · Carleton at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_o8yt.xml","label":"September 6 · Waterloo at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_jbsa.xml","label":"September 12 · Carleton at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_o7bu.xml","label":"September 19 · Queen's at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_yqpv.xml","label":"October 4 · Carleton at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_e02s.xml","label":"October 10 · Western at Carleton"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-waterloo-york","away":"waterloo","home":"york","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Warriors, Lions look to build on recent wins","paragraphs":["York's win over Ottawa gave it a way to survive an uneven passing day: keep the opponent to 12 points, then find enough offence on the ground. Doing that against Waterloo would make a much stronger argument that the result was a turning point.","Maurice Sodja was intercepted twice against the Gee-Gees, but rushed for 51 yards and a touchdown in the 19–12 win. The Lions had needed far more offence in their previous losses to Laurier and Windsor.","Waterloo comes with a similar recent experience but a different scoring total. Nick Orr threw two interceptions against Laurier, while Brandon Riggan's rushing and Tyler Tierney's receiving helped the Warriors find 39 points and a win.","That is roughly twice York's season scoring average, and it gives the Lions' defence a more demanding job than it had against Ottawa. Waterloo, however, has allowed 39.2 points a game, almost identical to York's 39.3.","Both teams have shown they can win without a clean passing performance. Their meeting will test whether either can make those wins easier to repeat by asking less of its offence when the ball changes hands."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_rmtf.xml","label":"August 29 · Ottawa at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_o8yt.xml","label":"September 6 · Waterloo at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_pii8.xml","label":"September 12 · Waterloo at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_ed0b.xml","label":"September 19 · Windsor at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_pvm1.xml","label":"September 26 · Waterloo at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_3xzq.xml","label":"October 3 · Laurier at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_y7d5.xml","label":"August 29 · Carleton at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_bmmb.xml","label":"September 6 · York at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_y44l.xml","label":"September 12 · McMaster at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_onmm.xml","label":"September 26 · York at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_dr1h.xml","label":"October 3 · York at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-10","label":"October 10 · Ottawa at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_kodd.xml","label":"2026-10-10 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-windsor-guelph","away":"windsor","home":"guelph","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Cotton, Aboud give Lancers-Gryphons plenty of intrigue","paragraphs":["Windsor's Kareame Cotton and Guelph's Tristan Aboud have drawn attention on the Hec Crighton Watch. Their most recent wins showed why the receivers catching their passes deserve some of it too.","Colby Ginn finished with 182 receiving yards and caught both of Cotton's touchdown passes in Windsor's 25–22 win over Queen's. It was a much closer game than the Lancers' previous wins over Toronto and York, making those catches important to more than the final passing total.","Guelph got two touchdown catches and 118 yards from Willem Arseneau against Toronto, part of a four-touchdown passing day for Aboud. The Gryphons won 46–0 to extend a three-game run in which they have scored 124 points.","That leaves both teams with reason to trust the passing game when they meet. Windsor has averaged 40.7 points and Guelph 37.2, so neither offence is accustomed to needing a perfect defensive afternoon to get a win.","The closer Windsor result may be the more useful comparison. Ginn helped the Lancers make their opportunities count against Queen's. If Guelph's defence keeps this game within reach, Cotton and Aboud may again need their receivers to make a few catches worth more than the rest."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_uxji.xml","label":"August 29 · Windsor at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_tqi8.xml","label":"September 6 · Laurier at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_nlwf.xml","label":"September 12 · Western at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_ed0b.xml","label":"September 19 · Windsor at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_1coy.xml","label":"September 26 · Toronto at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_dr1h.xml","label":"October 3 · York at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_11lr.xml","label":"October 10 · Windsor at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_zyoz.xml","label":"August 29 · Guelph at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_zejw.xml","label":"September 6 · McMaster at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_jbsa.xml","label":"September 12 · Carleton at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hkpj.xml","label":"September 19 · Guelph at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_pvm1.xml","label":"September 26 · Waterloo at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_07bf.xml","label":"October 3 · Guelph at Toronto"},{"url":"https://athletics.uwaterloo.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/windsor-lancers/boxscore/9407","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/laurier-golden-hawks/boxscore/6118","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/mcmaster-marauders/boxscore/6117","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/toronto-varsity-blues/boxscore/6121","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-mustangs/boxscore/6119","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/york-lions/boxscore/6122","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/carleton-ravens/boxscore/9559","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laurier-golden-hawks/boxscore/9557","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/mcmaster-marauders/boxscore/9558","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ottawa-gee-gees/boxscore/9560","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/toronto-varsity-blues/boxscore/9562","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-30-saskatchewan-ubc","away":"saskatchewan","home":"ubc","date":"2026-10-30","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Thunderbirds await return meeting with Huskies","paragraphs":["UBC got 137 rushing yards and a touchdown from Marvyn Larozar in its last meeting with Saskatchewan. It still lost by ten, a reminder that a good ground game does not leave much margin against the Huskies.","Saskatchewan won 34–24, getting two rushing touchdowns from Aulain Penner and 295 passing yards from Anton Amundrud. UBC's Drew Viotto threw two touchdown passes but was also intercepted twice, giving the Thunderbirds a productive afternoon with too many opportunities left behind.","That is what makes Larozar's role in the return meeting more interesting than his yardage alone. If his running helps UBC keep drives alive and avoid depending on difficult passing situations, it can change more than the balance of the offence.","The Huskies have been comfortable scoring through both Amundrud and the ground game, averaging 40.6 points through five outings. UBC has shown it can put points up against them too. The rematch gives the Thunderbirds a chance to turn that competitive performance into a different result by letting fewer possessions end in Saskatchewan's favour."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-30","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_gdvt.xml","label":"September 5 · Saskatchewan at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_mge2.xml","label":"September 18 · Saskatchewan at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_8tvd.xml","label":"October 3 · UBC at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_bx7n.xml","label":"September 4 · UBC at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_y81r.xml","label":"September 18 · Regina at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-british-columbia/boxscore/8947","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/9303","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/6999","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://www.reginacougars.com/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc/boxscore/11425","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-saskatchewan/boxscore/8948","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan-huskies/boxscore/9300","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan/boxscore/15527","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/regina-rams/boxscore/6998","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-30-sherbrooke-mcgill","away":"sherbrooke","home":"mcgill","date":"2026-10-30","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Vert & Or seek turnaround against Redbirds","paragraphs":["Sherbrooke's first meeting with McGill produced one point. Its next game produced 310 passing yards from Jeremy Fyfe and a six-point loss to Montréal, a much more encouraging version of an offence still searching for a win.","The return meeting with the Redbirds gives Sherbrooke a chance to show that the improvement can survive against a team that had previously shut it down. McGill won 34–1 in September, part of a three-game winning streak.","The Redbirds have been getting better returns from their own offensive work. Elliott Drapeau threw two touchdown passes and ran for another against Bishop's, helping McGill reach 47 points without asking the passing game to do everything.","Sherbrooke has averaged 16.4 points through five games, so Fyfe's yardage against Montréal was a useful step rather than a finished answer. He gave the Vert & Or enough movement to keep the game close. Against McGill, the next step is making that movement worth more than the single point the first meeting allowed."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-30","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Sherbrooke at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_8v74.xml","label":"September 26 · McGill at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_60uu.xml","label":"September 11 · Laval at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12458","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12462","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/concordia-shaughnessy-cup-/boxscore/12460","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laval-tva-/boxscore/12459","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/sherbrooke/boxscore/12461","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_zz6y.xml","label":"2026-10-03 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-30-stfx-saint-marys","away":"stfx","home":"saint-marys","date":"2026-10-30","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"X-Men, Huskies meet in AUS finale","paragraphs":["StFX has been winning with a scoring pace Saint Mary's rarely allows an opponent to reach. Their late-season meeting will test which team's recent experience travels better into a more difficult game.","The X-Men have scored 124 points during a three-game winning streak. Against Mount Allison, Deion Blackwood threw two touchdown passes and Aiden Rossong ran for two more, giving StFX more than one way to keep the scoreboard moving.","Saint Mary's has been able to win without needing that sort of total. The Huskies have allowed only 12.2 points a game, letting Malcolm Bussey's running help control contests rather than chase opponents who are already out of reach.","Bussey rushed for 124 yards and a touchdown against Acadia. His work would become even more useful against StFX if it keeps Blackwood and Rossong waiting for their next possession.","The X-Men have been good defensively too, allowing 15.8 points a game. That leaves both offences facing a version of the opponent that their recent results have not often required them to outscore. StFX has the larger scoring totals; Saint Mary's has been making smaller ones enough."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-30","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_olce.xml","label":"September 5 · Saint Mary's at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_s8sj.xml","label":"September 12 · Acadia at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_2r1j.xml","label":"September 19 · StFX at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_6175.xml","label":"September 26 · StFX at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_n4x7.xml","label":"October 3 · Mount Allison at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_aecb.xml","label":"September 11 · Mount Allison at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_vzdr.xml","label":"September 19 · Saint Mary's at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_e8ye.xml","label":"September 26 · Saint Mary's at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_b8gs.xml","label":"October 2 · Acadia at Saint Mary's"}]},{"id":"2026-10-31-bishops-concordia","away":"bishops","home":"concordia","date":"2026-10-31","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gaiters seek more offence in Stingers rematch","paragraphs":["Concordia needed only ten points to beat Bishop's in September. The Gaiters will want their improved passing game to make that a much less comfortable target in the rematch.","The 10–5 loss was followed by a 47–27 defeat against McGill, but Mathieu Bellavance threw two touchdown passes without an interception in that later game. Bishop's finally had more offence to work with, even if its defence did not let those points change the result.","Concordia has also found receiving production without finding enough scoring around it. Ely Rivest had 117 yards and a touchdown against Laval, only for the Stingers to lose 48–15.","That leaves two 1–4 teams with something more useful to bring into the return meeting than the memory of a 15-point game. Bellavance has shown he can finish drives through the air; Rivest has shown he can find space against a stronger opponent.","For Bishop's, the first of those developments is particularly important. The Gaiters do not need to turn this into a high-scoring game to change the result. They do need to give Concordia more to worry about than whether ten points will again be enough."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-31","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Sherbrooke at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_shbp.xml","label":"September 26 · Concordia at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_ppda.xml","label":"September 12 · Montréal at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12462","label":"2026-10-04 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-31-calgary-alberta","away":"calgary","home":"alberta","date":"2026-10-31","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Dinos look to answer Golden Bears in return game","paragraphs":["Calgary and Alberta combined for 77 points in September, and the Dinos still ended up seven short. Since then, Calgary has shown it can win a much quieter game. Alberta has shown how quickly its own offence can become quiet for the wrong reason.","The Dinos beat Regina 14–13 after the 42–35 loss to the Golden Bears. David Jordan passed for 215 yards without an interception, giving Calgary enough offensive stability to let a low-scoring game stay manageable.","Alberta's next outing went the other way. Eli Hetlinger was intercepted twice in an 18–3 loss to Manitoba, a sharp drop from the offence that had just beaten Calgary.","That leaves the return meeting less straightforward than the first score suggests. The Golden Bears have already proved they can trade touchdowns with the Dinos, but Calgary has also found a way to win without needing 35 points.","If Jordan can keep the passing game as clean as it was against Regina, Alberta may have to do more than reproduce a few of September's big offensive moments. It will have to make its own possessions last longer than they did against Manitoba."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-31","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_bx7n.xml","label":"September 4 · UBC at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_96n6.xml","label":"September 19 · Calgary at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260925_jbqx.xml","label":"September 25 · Alberta at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_pg8n.xml","label":"September 4 · Regina at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_mge2.xml","label":"September 18 · Saskatchewan at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/regina/boxscore/15530","label":"2026-10-03 · Official player box score"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-manitoba/boxscore/8950","label":"2026-10-02 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-31-laval-montreal","away":"laval","home":"montreal","date":"2026-10-31","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Carabins get another shot at Rouge et Or","paragraphs":["Montréal had 34 points the last time it played Laval and still finished eight short. The return meeting gives the Carabins another chance to make a good offensive day count against the Rouge et Or.","The 42–34 loss came in a game that left little room for either side to waste a scoring opportunity. Laval has continued at that pace, most recently getting three touchdown catches from Olivier Cool in a 48–15 win over Concordia.","Montréal's next win was less comfortable and less spectacular. Merton Theagene rushed for 116 yards against Sherbrooke as the Carabins worked through a 23–17 game, finding a result without approaching their usual scoring total.","That offers Montréal a useful alternative to simply trying to beat Laval in another exchange of touchdowns. If Theagene can help the Carabins sustain possessions, Victor Charland and Cool get fewer opportunities to make the return game look like the first.","The season averages show how little separates the offences: 39 points for Laval and 38.8 for Montréal. The first meeting showed how expensive even one additional successful drive can become when both teams can keep scoring."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-31","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_60uu.xml","label":"September 11 · Laval at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_3enl.xml","label":"September 26 · Montréal at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_ppda.xml","label":"September 12 · Montréal at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laval-tva-/boxscore/12459","label":"Victor Charland · player statistics"},{"url":"https://rougeetor.ulaval.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/boxscore-20260905-concordia-laval.pdf","label":"Victor Charland · player statistics"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_zz6y.xml","label":"2026-10-03 · Official player box score"}]},{"id":"2026-10-31-mount-allison-acadia","away":"mount-allison","home":"acadia","date":"2026-10-31","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Mounties, Axemen renew matchup in Wolfville","paragraphs":["Mount Allison found 30 points against Acadia in September. Neither team has made scoring look that easy very often since, giving the Axemen a clear place to start when they get the return game at home.","The Mounties won the opener between them 30–13, but have averaged only 15.4 points through five games. Acadia has been quieter still at 14.4, with both sides facing difficult stretches against Saint Mary's and StFX.","There has been receiving production to work with. Quinten George had 96 yards for Mount Allison against the X-Men, while Acadia's Jase LeBlanc finished with 104 yards and a touchdown against the Huskies. In both cases, those catches came without enough scoring elsewhere to keep the game close.","That is why the first meeting stands out. Mount Allison turned its opportunities into a total that its other recent opponents have not allowed it to repeat. Acadia now has to keep that from becoming the pattern between these two teams, while making LeBlanc's receiving part of a more productive offence of its own."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-31","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_m54m.xml","label":"September 4 · Acadia at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_aecb.xml","label":"September 11 · Mount Allison at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_2r1j.xml","label":"September 19 · StFX at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_e8ye.xml","label":"September 26 · Saint Mary's at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_n4x7.xml","label":"October 3 · Mount Allison at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_s8sj.xml","label":"September 12 · Acadia at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_vzdr.xml","label":"September 19 · Saint Mary's at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_6175.xml","label":"September 26 · StFX at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_b8gs.xml","label":"October 2 · Acadia at Saint Mary's"}]},{"id":"2026-10-31-regina-manitoba","away":"regina","home":"manitoba","date":"2026-10-31","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Rams, Bisons prepare for another close contest","paragraphs":["Regina has been running well enough to keep games close. Manitoba's latest win showed what can happen when a productive ground game is paired with a cleaner passing afternoon.","Carter Ashman rushed for 110 yards in the Rams' 14–13 loss to Calgary, but Owen Sieben was intercepted three times. That left Regina with its third straight narrow defeat and another reason to wonder how much more it needed to get from a game still within reach.","The Bisons had a different experience against Alberta. Ishe Matanga rushed for 122 yards, while Cole Anseeuw threw a touchdown without an interception in an 18–3 win. Manitoba did not need a large passing total because its offence avoided asking the defence to rescue too many lost possessions.","That makes the matchup more than a comparison between Ashman and Matanga's rushing yards. Both have shown they can give their teams useful work on the ground. The difference will be how much of it survives the rest of the drive. Regina has been finding enough yards to stay close; Manitoba has a recent example of turning that kind of afternoon into a win."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-31","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_pg8n.xml","label":"September 4 · Regina at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_hvcf.xml","label":"September 11 · Manitoba at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_y81r.xml","label":"September 18 · Regina at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_gdvt.xml","label":"September 5 · Saskatchewan at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_96n6.xml","label":"September 19 · Calgary at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/regina/boxscore/15530","label":"2026-10-03 · Official player box score"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-manitoba/boxscore/8950","label":"2026-10-02 · Official player box score"}]}]};
